WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:09.216
If you had to walk on hot sand with a heavy backpack and no water to drink, how

2
00:00:09.316 --> 00:00:10.377
long could you walk?

3
00:00:11.157 --> 00:00:12.899
Could you walk for ten minutes?

4
00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:15.341
Could you walk for one hour?

5
00:00:16.302 --> 00:00:18.123
Could you walk for three weeks?

6
00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:21.706
There is one animal that can: the camel!

7
00:00:24.209 --> 00:00:27.812
There are two kinds of camels, the Dromedary and the Bactrian.

8
00:00:28.584 --> 00:00:32.867
Dromedary camels have only one hump and Bactrian camels have two.

9
00:00:33.608 --> 00:00:38.611
If you turn the letters D and B on their sides, this will help you remember their names.

10
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:44.695
Dromedary camels live in Arabia, India, and North Africa.

11
00:00:45.316 --> 00:00:51.400
There are 13 million Dromedary camels alive today, and all of them are used to carry loads through

12
00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:52.020
the desert.

13
00:00:52.701 --> 00:00:57.324
Because they are so valuable to humans, there are no more wild Dromedary camels.

14
00:00:59.964 --> 00:01:03.567
Bactrian camels live in China, Mongolia, and Kazakhstan.

15
00:01:04.628 --> 00:01:09.152
Scientists are worried because there are not many wild Bactrian camels left in the world.

16
00:01:09.952 --> 00:01:12.915
There are only 950 living in the Gobi Desert.

17
00:01:14.436 --> 00:01:20.541
Bactrian camels are slower than Dromedary camels, so people prefer Dromedaries.

18
00:01:22.282 --> 00:01:23.944
Do you wish you had a camel?

19
00:01:24.504 --> 00:01:26.146
If you do, listen to this.

20
00:01:26.886 --> 00:01:28.828
Camels are very difficult pets.

21
00:01:29.196 --> 00:01:32.679
They like to bite, spit, and kick people who make them work.

22
00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:40.065
Camels eat 12 kilograms of food every day and can drink 114 liters of water in ten minutes!

23
00:01:41.306 --> 00:01:43.928
But there are a lot of good things about camels too.

24
00:01:44.669 --> 00:01:46.490
Camel milk is very delicious.

25
00:01:47.071 --> 00:01:49.293
And camel wool can be made into clothes.

26
00:01:50.353 --> 00:01:53.316
If you need to light a fire, you can use camel dung.

27
00:01:54.917 --> 00:01:58.140
These three camel gifts help people survive in the desert.

28
00:02:00.016 --> 00:02:01.678
But wait, there is more!

29
00:02:02.298 --> 00:02:07.462
Camels are called ships of the desert because they carry very big loads from one side of the

30
00:02:07.522 --> 00:02:08.563
desert to the other.

31
00:02:09.564 --> 00:02:13.627
Dromedary camels can carry over two hundred kilograms on their backs.

32
00:02:15.789 --> 00:02:19.152
Camels walk four kilometers per hour through the hot desert.

33
00:02:20.013 --> 00:02:22.855
They can go like this for three weeks without water!

34
00:02:23.455 --> 00:02:24.316
That's amazing!

35
00:02:25.257 --> 00:02:26.738
Why don't camels need water?

36
00:02:28.079 --> 00:02:30.669
Here's a hint: they don't store it in their humps.

37
00:02:31.489 --> 00:02:34.490
Camels do need water, but they save it for long trips.

38
00:02:35.771 --> 00:02:39.772
For example, when the weather gets hot, camels don't sweat much.

39
00:02:40.393 --> 00:02:42.734
Instead, they let their bodies get warmer.

40
00:02:44.494 --> 00:02:49.456
Even when camels go to the bathroom, they save their water and only lose the waste.

41
00:02:50.537 --> 00:02:54.919
A camel can lose up to 40 percent of its body's water before getting sick.

42
00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:58.964
Humans can lose only 20 percent.

43
00:02:58.984 --> 00:03:03.007
These are just some of the reasons that camels don't need water in the desert.

44
00:03:04.849 --> 00:03:07.010
So what is in the camel's hump?

45
00:03:07.811 --> 00:03:08.551
Good question.

46
00:03:08.952 --> 00:03:12.154
When camels are not walking, they eat a lot of food.

47
00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:16.757
Their bodies turn the food into fat and save the fat in their humps.

48
00:03:17.658 --> 00:03:20.560
The fat helps them walk for many weeks without eating.

49
00:03:22.041 --> 00:03:25.444
The next time you see a picture of a camel, look at its hump.

50
00:03:26.140 --> 00:03:29.163
If the hump is tall, it means the camel is healthy.

51
00:03:29.883 --> 00:03:35.488
If the hump is short or falling over, it means the camel needs a vacation and lots to

52
00:03:35.588 --> 00:03:36.489
eat and drink!

53
00:03:39.071 --> 00:03:40.653
Camels are amazing animals.

54
00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.315
They can close their noses in sandstorms.

55
00:03:43.955 --> 00:03:46.458
They can eat thorn bushes without hurting their lips.

56
00:03:47.118 --> 00:03:49.080
They can live to be forty years old.

57
00:03:49.961 --> 00:03:56.054
It's no wonder the Bedouin, the desert people of northern Africa, call camels the gift of God!
